{
  "summary": "This multimodal experiment (single profile, PCA n2000 RNA, ResNet50 image, concat fusion) achieved a validation accuracy of 0.527 (F1: 0.510), a ~4.2-point improvement over the RNA-only baseline (0.485, F1: 0.464) from llm_summary_001. Because the only change relative to that baseline was the addition of the image modality with ResNet50 and concat fusion, the result suggests that incorporating image features provides predictive signal beyond RNA alone under this minimal configuration. However, the relative contributions of the image encoder architecture versus the concat fusion strategy remain unisolated, and it is uncertain whether alternative encoders or more sophisticated fusion mechanisms could yield further gains."
}

